#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""apply-edits -- apply an integrator EDIT_LIST exactly, or not at all (corp department 7, "Apply + verify").

Every EDIT_LIST row already carries its verbatim `old` and `new`, so applying it is fully determined work: it belongs
to code, not to a model. This script replaces the model applier. The fresh verifier that re-extracts the rebuilt
artifact and asserts the CLAIM (not the patch) stays a model seat -- a matched anchor is not proof.

USAGE
  apply-edits EDIT_LIST.json --out-dir DIR [--stamp S] [--root DIR] [--backup-dir DIR] [--dry-run]   # edited copies
  apply-edits EDIT_LIST.json --in-place    [--stamp S] [--root DIR] [--backup-dir DIR] [--dry-run]   # dated backups first
  apply-edits EDIT_LIST.json --dry-run     [--root DIR]                                              # check only, no writes
  EDIT_LIST.json may be '-' (stdin). Run from anywhere; python3 + stdlib, python-docx only for .docx targets.

BUILD STAMP (D4; doctrine rule 20)
  --stamp S      Every .docx this run writes gets docProps/core.xml <cp:lastModifiedBy> = S and <dcterms:modified> = the
                 build time (UTC), and the md5 receipts are taken from the stamped bytes. A python-docx build from a human's
                 .docx otherwise keeps THAT person's name and save time, and share-check.sh reads our build as their Office
                 save (a false HUMAN EDIT, or our edit disguised as the pre-campaign base). A write that includes a .docx
                 and has no --stamp exits 2 naming the choices: share-check.sh's own BUILD_STAMPS, read from that script
                 (never a copy). For a Acme payer build S must be one of them exactly; a stamp beginning "Acme Org"
                 that is not exact exits 2. Any other non-blank stamp is allowed with a warning: share-check will read it
                 as a human's save. --dry-run and check mode need no stamp (they warn when a write would).

INPUT
  The kit's EDIT_LIST ({"edits": [...], "deferred": [...], "rejected": [...]}) or a bare array of edits.
  Each edit: {"id", "file", "old", "new", "expect"?: int >= 1 (default 1), "kind"?: "mechanical" | "judgment"}.
  Other fields (closes, rationale, jev_*) are ignored; deferred[] and rejected[] are counted, never applied.
  `file`: absolute, `~/...`, or relative to --root (default: the current directory).

MODES
  --out-dir DIR  Non-destructive: edited copies go under DIR, mirroring each file's path relative to --root (without
                 --root: relative to the target files' common parent directory). Originals are never opened for
                 writing. A copy that already exists in DIR is backed up first (<copy>.bak-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS).
  --in-place     Edits the files themselves, only after a verified dated backup of every file it changes
                 (<file>.bak-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS beside it, or mirrored under --backup-dir; an existing backup name is
                 never reused: -2, -3 ...). Refuses (exit 2, nothing written) if any backup cannot be written, if a
                 file changed on disk after it was read, if a file is read-only, or if Word has a .docx open (~$
                 lock file). Permissions are kept; a symlinked path edits the file it points to.
  --dry-run      Computes and reports everything, writes nothing (alone = check the list against the files).

RULES
  Per file, edits apply in list order to the CURRENT text. An edit applies only when `old` occurs exactly `expect`
  times; every occurrence is replaced. Otherwise it is a MISS -- not found · found N != expect · file missing /
  unreadable / unsupported · overlaps an earlier edit (an earlier edit changed text `old` matched, or the match
  falls on text an earlier edit wrote: never chained, never fuzzy-matched) · occurrences overlap each other
  ("aa" in "aaa") · no-op (new == old) · kind "judgment" (a named human decides; never applied mechanically).
  Matching is exact, code point by code point: no whitespace, line-ending, Unicode or case normalisation. A MISS
  carries a `hint` -- e.g. the same text after whitespace / Unicode / case normalisation, with the first differing
  character named -- that is NEVER applied.
  ATOMIC: one miss and nothing is written. Fix the list, re-run against the untouched originals.
  POST-CHECK: before writing, the rebuilt bytes are re-extracted and must equal the expected text; after writing,
  every changed file is re-read from disk, byte-compared and re-extracted, and each applied `new` must be present
  exactly the expected number of times. Any failure is a MISS.

.docx (needs python-docx; without it a .docx edit is a MISS naming the interpreter)
  Matches within one paragraph's visible text: body, tables, text boxes, content controls, hyperlinks, fields'
  shown results, tracked insertions, headers, footers, footnotes, endnotes. Tracked deletions, comments and
  legacy text-box fallback copies are not matched (a fallback copy is synced when it is an exact twin). Tab = "\\t",
  line break = "\\n"; a paragraph break is not a character, so `old` never spans paragraphs. Only the CHANGED text
  is rewritten (the prefix/suffix that old and new share is left alone). Changed text inside one run keeps that
  run's formatting exactly; changed text spanning runs is applied at paragraph level (the new text takes the first
  run's formatting, text outside the match keeps its runs) and is reported in `formatting_risk`, as is non-text
  content (drawing, field code, page break) inside the changed span or a hyperlink/field boundary it crosses.

OUTPUT
  stdout: one JSON report -- ok, exit, mode, dry_run, written, stamp, applied[] (ids on disk and post-checked),
  misses[{id, file, reason, hint?}], files_changed[], backups[{file, backup}], matched[] (ids that applied in
  memory), outputs[{file, output, status, md5_before, md5_after, chars/words before/after, stamped?}],
  formatting_risk[{id, file, location, runs, same_formatting, detail}], warnings[], counts{}; on exit 2 also `error`.
  stderr: one line per miss and per risk, a summary, then the final line `MISSES (n)`.
EXIT
  0 no misses · 1 any miss (a build failure; a pre-write miss writes nothing, a post-check miss names the written
  files and their backups) · 2 bad input or a refused run, nothing written; final stderr line `BAD INPUT: ...` or
  `REFUSED: ...` (never `MISSES (0)`).
"""
import argparse
import ast
import hashlib
import io
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import sys
import tempfile
import time
import unicodedata
from datetime import datetime, timezone

EXIT_OK, EXIT_MISS, EXIT_BAD = 0, 1, 2
HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
ORG_PREFIX = "Acme Org"
BUILD_STAMPS_RE = re.compile(r"^\s*BUILD_STAMPS\s*=\s*(\{[^}\n]*\})", re.M)

# Formats that are not plain text and are not the one Office format this script edits: a byte-level replace
# inside them would corrupt the file or silently miss, so they are refused by name.
UNSUPPORTED_EXT = {".pdf", ".doc", ".docm", ".dotx", ".dotm", ".rtf", ".xlsx", ".xlsm", ".xls", ".pptx", ".pptm",
                   ".ppt", ".odt", ".ods", ".odp", ".pages", ".zip", ".png", ".jpg", ".jpeg", ".gif", ".webp",
                   ".heic", ".tif", ".tiff"}
MAX_LOCS = 5


class BadInput(Exception):
    """Exit 2: the invocation or the edit list is malformed. Nothing is written."""


class Refused(Exception):
    """Exit 2: writing would be unsafe (no backup possible, file changed underneath, Word lock). Nothing written."""


class SurgeryError(Exception):
    """A .docx paragraph edit did not reproduce the expected paragraph text (internal; the file is abandoned)."""


class DocxUnavailable(Exception):
    pass


class _Parser(argparse.ArgumentParser):
    def error(self, message):
        raise BadInput(message)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Small helpers


def md5(data):
    return hashlib.md5(data).hexdigest()


def share_check_path():
    # CORP_SHARE_CHECK: test-only override. The stamps are read from share-check.sh itself, never copied (D4).
    return os.environ.get("CORP_SHARE_CHECK") or os.path.join(HERE, "share-check.sh")


def build_stamps():
    """share-check.sh's exact BUILD_STAMPS set -> (sorted list, None) or (None, why it could not be read)."""
    path = share_check_path()
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            m = BUILD_STAMPS_RE.search(fh.read())
        if not m:
            return None, "no BUILD_STAMPS = {...} line in %s" % path
        stamps = ast.literal_eval(m.group(1))
        if not isinstance(stamps, set) or not stamps or not all(isinstance(s, str) and s.strip() for s in stamps):
            return None, "BUILD_STAMPS in %s is not a set of non-empty strings" % path
        return sorted(stamps), None
    except (OSError, ValueError, SyntaxError) as ex:
        return None, "cannot read BUILD_STAMPS from %s: %s" % (path, ex)


def check_stamp(stamp, writes_docx, rep):
    """D4: validate --stamp against share-check.sh's BUILD_STAMPS. BadInput when a .docx write has none, when it is blank or
    too long, or when a Acme stamp is not exact; a warning for any other stamp (share-check reads it as a human)."""
    stamps, why = build_stamps()
    choices = ("one of share-check.sh's BUILD_STAMPS -- the one naming this deliverable's track (FA-13): "
               + " | ".join("'%s'" % s for s in stamps)) if stamps else \
        "share-check.sh's BUILD_STAMPS could not be read (%s)" % why
    if stamp is None:
        if writes_docx:
            raise BadInput("this run writes a .docx: pass --stamp with the build identity for its lastModifiedBy -- %s "
                           "(rule 20: a build from a human's .docx must never keep their name)" % choices)
        return
    if not stamp.strip():
        raise BadInput("--stamp is blank: lastModifiedBy is never blank (rail 14) -- %s" % choices)
    if len(stamp) > 255:
        raise BadInput("--stamp is %d characters; docProps/core.xml allows 255" % len(stamp))
    if stamps and stamp in stamps:
        return
    if stamp.strip().lower().startswith(ORG_PREFIX.lower()):
        raise BadInput("--stamp %r looks like a Acme build stamp but is not exact -- %s" % (stamp, choices))
    rep.warnings.append("--stamp %r is not one of share-check.sh's BUILD_STAMPS: share-check will read this build as a "
                        "human's Office save (fine outside a Acme payer build; there, use %s)" % (stamp, choices))


def read_bytes(path):
    with open(path, "rb") as fh:
        return fh.read()


def _timestamp():
    return time.strftime("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S", time.localtime())


def find_all(hay, needle):
    """Every start position of needle in hay, overlapping ones included (str.count would hide 'aa' in 'aaa')."""
    out = []
    i = hay.find(needle)
    while i != -1:
        out.append(i)
        i = hay.find(needle, i + 1)
    return out


def cname(ch):
    """U+00A0 NO-BREAK SPACE -- a character named so an invisible difference is visible in a hint."""
    name = unicodedata.name(ch, "<control>" if unicodedata.category(ch) == "Cc" else "<unnamed>")
    shown = " '%s'" % ch if (ch.isprintable() and not ch.isspace()) else ""
    return "U+%04X %s%s" % (ord(ch), name, shown)


def visible(s, limit=160):
    """Quote file text for a hint: invisible or unusual whitespace becomes an escape; long text is cut."""
    out = []
    for ch in s:
        if ch == " " or (ch.isprintable() and not ch.isspace()):
            out.append(ch)
        elif ch == "\n":
            out.append("\\n")
        elif ch == "\t":
            out.append("\\t")
        elif ch == "\r":
            out.append("\\r")
        else:
            out.append("\\u%04x" % ord(ch) if ord(ch) <= 0xFFFF else "\\U%08x" % ord(ch))
    text = "".join(out)
    if len(text) > limit:
        text = text[:limit] + "..."
    return '"' + text + '"'


def xml_bad_char(s):
    """First character XML 1.0 cannot hold (so a .docx cannot either), or None."""
    for ch in s:
        o = ord(ch)
        if ch in "\t\n\r" or 0x20 <= o <= 0xD7FF or 0xE000 <= o <= 0xFFFD or 0x10000 <= o <= 0x10FFFF:
            continue
        return ch
    return None


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hint normalisation -- used ONLY to explain a miss, never to apply anything.

INVISIBLE = {"\u200b", "\u200c", "\u200d", "\u2060", "\ufeff", "\u00ad"}
TYPO = {"\u2018": "'", "\u2019": "'", "\u201a": "'", "\u201b": "'", "\u2032": "'", "\u00b4": "'",
        "\u201c": '"', "\u201d": '"', "\u201e": '"', "\u201f": '"', "\u2033": '"', "\u00ab": '"', "\u00bb": '"',
        "\u2010": "-", "\u2011": "-", "\u2012": "-", "\u2013": "-", "\u2014": "-", "\u2015": "-", "\u2212": "-",
        "\u2026": "..."}
LEVELS = ((1, "whitespace"), (2, "Unicode/typography (NFKD, quotes, dashes) + whitespace"),
          (3, "letter-case + Unicode + whitespace"))


def norm_map(s, level):
    """Normalised text plus, for each normalised char, the index of the source char it came from."""
    out, idx, prev_space = [], [], False
    for i, ch in enumerate(s):
        if ch in INVISIBLE:
            continue
        seq = ch
        if level >= 2:
            seq = TYPO.get(ch) or unicodedata.normalize("NFKD", ch)
        for c in seq:
            if c.isspace():
                if prev_space:
                    continue
                out.append(" ")
                idx.append(i)
                prev_space = True
            else:
                for cc in (c.casefold() if level >= 3 else c):
                    out.append(cc)
                    idx.append(i)
                prev_space = False
    return "".join(out), idx


def first_diff(old, actual):
    for i in range(min(len(old), len(actual))):
        if old[i] != actual[i]:
            return "first difference at old[%d]: old has %s, the file has %s" % (i, cname(old[i]), cname(actual[i]))
    if len(old) > len(actual):
        return "old has %d extra trailing char(s) starting %s" % (len(old) - len(actual), cname(old[len(actual)]))
    if len(actual) > len(old):
        return "the file has %d extra char(s) starting %s" % (len(actual) - len(old), cname(actual[len(old)]))
    return "no character difference"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The text model shared by both engines: a document is a list of segments (the whole file for text; one per
# paragraph for .docx). A segment keeps its original string, its current string and the replacements applied so
# far in ORIGINAL coordinates, which is what makes "overlaps an earlier edit" exact rather than guessed.


class Segment(object):
    def __init__(self, orig, label=None, para=None):
        self.orig = orig
        self.cur = orig
        self.reps = []          # (orig_start, orig_end, new, edit_id), sorted, non-overlapping
        self.label = label
        self.para = para        # .docx: the w:p element
        self.twin = None        # .docx: the legacy fallback copy of a text-box paragraph (element), False if unpairable
        self.twin_expected = None

    def dirty(self):
        """Current-coordinate spans written by earlier edits: (start, end, edit_id); end == start for a deletion."""
        out, shift = [], 0
        for (o_start, o_end, new, eid) in self.reps:
            c = o_start + shift
            out.append((c, c + len(new), eid))
            shift += len(new) - (o_end - o_start)
        return out

    def to_orig(self, a):
        shift = 0
        for (o_start, o_end, new, eid) in self.reps:
            c = o_start + shift
            if c + len(new) <= a:
                shift += len(new) - (o_end - o_start)
            else:
                break
        return a - shift

    def replace(self, a, b, new, eid):
        o_a = self.to_orig(a)
        rep = (o_a, o_a + (b - a), new, eid)
        i = 0
        while i < len(self.reps) and self.reps[i][0] < o_a:
            i += 1
        self.reps.insert(i, rep)
        self.cur = self.cur[:a] + new + self.cur[b:]

    def rebuilt(self):
        """The current text recomputed from the original + the replacement ledger (an independent code path)."""
        parts, pos = [], 0
        for (o_start, o_end, new, eid) in self.reps:
            parts.append(self.orig[pos:o_start])
            parts.append(new)
            pos = o_end
        parts.append(self.orig[pos:])
        return "".join(parts)


class TextDoc(object):
    kind = "text"

    def __init__(self, data):
        self.segments = [Segment(data.decode("utf-8"))]
        self.broken = None

    def where(self, seg, pos):
        line = seg.cur.count("\n", 0, pos) + 1
        col = pos - (seg.cur.rfind("\n", 0, pos) + 1) + 1
        return "line %d col %d" % (line, col)

    def edit(self, seg, a, b, new):
        return None, None     # the string model is the whole story for a text file

    def serialize(self):
        return self.segments[0].cur.encode("utf-8")

    def expected(self):
        return [(None, self.segments[0].cur, None)]

    @staticmethod
    def extract(data):
        return [(None, data.decode("utf-8"), None)]


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .docx engine (python-docx for the package, lxml for the paragraph surgery)

W_NS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"
MC_NS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"


def _w(tag):
    return "{%s}%s" % (W_NS, tag)


W_P, W_R, W_T, W_TAB, W_PTAB, W_BR, W_CR, W_NBH = (_w("p"), _w("r"), _w("t"), _w("tab"), _w("ptab"), _w("br"),
                                                    _w("cr"), _w("noBreakHyphen"))
W_PPR, W_RPR, W_DEL, W_MOVEFROM, W_TXBX, W_TC = (_w("pPr"), _w("rPr"), _w("del"), _w("moveFrom"),
                                                 _w("txbxContent"), _w("tc"))
W_LRPB, W_TYPE = _w("lastRenderedPageBreak"), _w("type")
MC_CHOICE, MC_FALLBACK = "{%s}Choice" % MC_NS, "{%s}Fallback" % MC_NS
XML_SPACE = "{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}space"
SPECIAL = {W_TAB: "\t", W_PTAB: "\t", W_CR: "\n", W_NBH: "-"}       # python-docx's own text for these
SKIP_SUBTREE = {W_PPR, W_RPR, W_DEL, W_MOVEFROM, MC_FALLBACK, W_P, W_TXBX}

_DOCX = None


def load_docx():
    """python-docx, imported on first .docx use; footnotes/endnotes registered as XML parts so they can be edited."""
    global _DOCX
    if _DOCX is None:
        try:
            import docx
            from docx.opc.constants import CONTENT_TYPE as CT
            from docx.opc.constants import RELATIONSHIP_TYPE as RT
            from docx.opc.part import PartFactory, XmlPart
            from docx.oxml import OxmlElement
            from lxml import etree
        except Exception as ex:   # ImportError, or a broken install
            _DOCX = ex
        else:
            PartFactory.part_type_for.setdefault(CT.WML_FOOTNOTES, XmlPart)
            PartFactory.part_type_for.setdefault(CT.WML_ENDNOTES, XmlPart)
            _DOCX = {"docx": docx, "RT": RT, "OxmlElement": OxmlElement, "etree": etree}
    if isinstance(_DOCX, Exception):
        raise DocxUnavailable("docx support unavailable: python-docx is not importable under %s (%s: %s)"
                              % (sys.executable, type(_DOCX).__name__, _DOCX))
    return _DOCX


def _inside(el, root, tag):
    node = el.getparent()
    while node is not None and node is not root:
        if node.tag == tag:
            return True
        node = node.getparent()
    return False


def run_elements(p):
    """The w:r elements that belong to paragraph p, in document order (not nested paragraphs, not deletions)."""
    out = []

    def visit(node):
        for child in node:
            tag = child.tag
            if not isinstance(tag, str):
                continue
            if tag == W_R:
                out.append(child)
            elif tag in SKIP_SUBTREE:
                continue
            else:                   # hyperlink, ins, moveTo, sdt/sdtContent, smartTag, customXml, fldSimple, ...
                visit(child)

    visit(p)
    return out


class Atom(object):
    __slots__ = ("el", "run", "text", "start", "end", "is_t")

    def __init__(self, el, run, text, start, is_t):
        self.el, self.run, self.text, self.start, self.end, self.is_t = el, run, text, start, start + len(text), is_t


def _atom_text(child):
    tag = child.tag
    if tag == W_T:
        return child.text or "", True
    if tag == W_BR:
        return ("\n" if child.get(W_TYPE) in (None, "textWrapping") else None), False
    if tag in SPECIAL:
        return SPECIAL[tag], False
    return None, False


def atoms_of(p):
    atoms, pos = [], 0
    for r in run_elements(p):
        for child in r:
            text, is_t = _atom_text(child)
            if not text:
                continue
            atoms.append(Atom(child, r, text, pos, is_t))
            pos += len(text)
    return atoms


def para_text(p):
    return "".join(a.text for a in atoms_of(p))


def _set_t(t, text):
    t.text = text
    if any(c.isspace() for c in text):
        t.set(XML_SPACE, "preserve")


def _content(text, ox):
    """w:t / w:tab / w:br elements that render `text` inside a run."""
    els, buf = [], []

    def flush():
        if buf:
            t = ox["OxmlElement"]("w:t")
            _set_t(t, "".join(buf))
            els.append(t)
            del buf[:]

    i = 0
    while i < len(text):
        ch = text[i]
        if ch == "\t":
            flush()
            els.append(ox["OxmlElement"]("w:tab"))
        elif ch in "\r\n":
            flush()
            els.append(ox["OxmlElement"]("w:br"))
            if ch == "\r" and text[i + 1:i + 2] == "\n":
                i += 1
        else:
            buf.append(ch)
        i += 1
    flush()
    return els


def _qname(tag):
    if not isinstance(tag, str):
        return "?"
    ns, _, local = tag[1:].partition("}") if tag.startswith("{") else ("", "", tag)
    return {W_NS: "w:", MC_NS: "mc:"}.get(ns, "") + local


def para_surgery(p, a, b, new, ox):
    """Replace paragraph-text span [a, b) with `new`, touching only the text elements it covers.

    One run covered: that run's formatting is untouched. Several runs: `new` goes into the first covered run, the
    covered text of the others is removed, text outside the match keeps its runs; returns a risk dict."""
    atoms = atoms_of(p)
    covered = [x for x in atoms if x.end > a and x.start < b]
    if not covered or covered[0].start > a or covered[-1].end < b:
        raise SurgeryError("span %d-%d does not map onto the paragraph's text elements" % (a, b))
    first, last = covered[0], covered[-1]
    prefix = first.text[:a - first.start]
    suffix = last.text[b - last.start:]
    runs = []
    for x in covered:
        if not any(x.run is r for r in runs):
            runs.append(x.run)

    # Anything that is not text inside the matched span (drawings, field codes, page breaks, notes references) and
    # whether the span crosses a container (hyperlink, field, content control, tracked change): reported, kept.
    all_runs = run_elements(p)
    i0 = next(i for i, r in enumerate(all_runs) if r is runs[0])
    i1 = next(i for i, r in enumerate(all_runs) if r is runs[-1])
    embedded = []
    for i in range(i0, i1 + 1):
        kids = list(all_runs[i])
        lo = next(k for k, c in enumerate(kids) if c is first.el) + 1 if i == i0 else 0
        hi = next(k for k, c in enumerate(kids) if c is last.el) if i == i1 else len(kids)
        for c in kids[lo:hi]:
            if c.tag in (W_RPR, W_LRPB) or not isinstance(c.tag, str):
                continue
            text, _ = _atom_text(c)
            if text is None:                  # drawing, field code, page/column break, note reference, ...
                embedded.append(_qname(c.tag))
    parents = []
    for r in all_runs[i0:i1 + 1]:
        par = r.getparent()
        if not any(par is q for q in parents):
            parents.append(par)
    risk = None
    if len(runs) > 1 or embedded or len(parents) > 1:
        keys = set()
        for r in runs:
            rpr = r.find(W_RPR)
            keys.add(b"" if rpr is None else ox["etree"].tostring(rpr))
        risk = {"runs": len(runs), "same_formatting": len(keys) <= 1, "boundary": len(parents) > 1,
                "embedded": sorted(set(embedded))}

    if first is last:
        if first.is_t and not any(c in new for c in "\t\r\n"):
            _set_t(first.el, prefix + new + suffix)
        else:
            for el in _content(prefix + new + suffix, ox):
                first.el.addprevious(el)
            first.el.getparent().remove(first.el)
    else:
        for el in _content(prefix + new, ox):
            first.el.addprevious(el)
        for el in _content(suffix, ox):
            last.el.addprevious(el)
        for x in covered:
            x.el.getparent().remove(x.el)
    return risk


def para_replace(p, text, a, b, new, ox):
    """Minimal-change form of para_surgery: the prefix and suffix that old and new share are left untouched, so a
    long anchor that crosses runs only disturbs formatting when the CHANGED text does. A pure insertion is hosted by
    a neighbouring character inside the match (the one before it, or the first char when inserting at the start)."""
    old = text[a:b]
    m = min(len(old), len(new))
    pre = 0
    while pre < m and old[pre] == new[pre]:
        pre += 1
    suf = 0
    while suf < m - pre and old[len(old) - 1 - suf] == new[len(new) - 1 - suf]:
        suf += 1
    a2, b2, mid = a + pre, b - suf, new[pre:len(new) - suf]
    if a2 == b2:
        if a2 > a:
            return para_surgery(p, a2 - 1, a2, text[a2 - 1] + mid, ox)
        return para_surgery(p, a2, a2 + 1, mid + text[a2], ox)
    return para_surgery(p, a2, b2, mid, ox)


def _fallback_twin(p, root):
    """The legacy (mc:Fallback) copy of a text-box paragraph that lives in an mc:Choice, else None/False."""
    node = p.getparent()
    while node is not None and node is not root and node.tag != MC_CHOICE:
        node = node.getparent()
    if node is None or node is root:
        return None
    fallbacks = [c for c in node.getparent() if c.tag == MC_FALLBACK]
    if not fallbacks:
        return None
    choice_ps = list(node.iter(W_P))
    fallback_ps = list(fallbacks[0].iter(W_P))
    if len(choice_ps) != len(fallback_ps):
        return False
    return fallback_ps[next(i for i, q in enumerate(choice_ps) if q is p)]


def _story_roots(document, ox):
    """(partname, root element) for the body, then headers, footers, footnotes, endnotes -- each part once."""
    RT = ox["RT"]
    rank = {RT.HEADER: 1, RT.FOOTER: 2, RT.FOOTNOTES: 3, RT.ENDNOTES: 4}
    main = document.part
    roots, seen, extra = [(str(main.partname), main.element)], {str(main.partname)}, []
    for rel in main.rels.values():
        if rel.is_external or rel.reltype not in rank:
            continue
        part = rel.target_part
        name = str(part.partname)
        el = getattr(part, "element", None) if hasattr(type(part), "element") else None
        if name in seen or el is None:
            continue
        seen.add(name)
        extra.append((rank[rel.reltype], name, el))
    extra.sort(key=lambda t: (t[0], len(t[1]), t[1]))
    return roots + [(name, el) for (_, name, el) in extra]


def collect_segments(document, ox):
    segs = []
    for partname, root in _story_roots(document, ox):
        short = partname.rsplit("/", 1)[-1]
        n = 0
        for p in list(root.iter(W_P)):
            if _inside(p, root, MC_FALLBACK):
                continue
            n += 1
            ctx = [name for tag, name in ((W_TC, "table"), (W_TXBX, "text box")) if _inside(p, root, tag)]
            seg = Segment(para_text(p), label="%s paragraph %d%s" % (short, n, " (%s)" % ", ".join(ctx) if ctx else ""),
                          para=p)
            seg.twin = _fallback_twin(p, root)
            if seg.twin is not None and seg.twin is not False:
                seg.twin_expected = para_text(seg.twin)
            segs.append(seg)
    return segs


class DocxDoc(object):
    kind = "docx"

    def __init__(self, data):
        self.ox = load_docx()
        self.document = self.ox["docx"].Document(io.BytesIO(data))
        self.segments = collect_segments(self.document, self.ox)
        self.broken = None
        self.stamp = None       # D4: set by the run; every serialized copy carries it as lastModifiedBy

    def where(self, seg, pos):
        return "%s col %d" % (seg.label, pos + 1)

    def edit(self, seg, a, b, new):
        """XML surgery for one occurrence, checked against the string model before the model moves."""
        expect_text = seg.cur[:a] + new + seg.cur[b:]
        risk = para_replace(seg.para, seg.cur, a, b, new, self.ox)
        got = para_text(seg.para)
        if got != expect_text:
            raise SurgeryError("%s reads %s after the edit, expected %s" % (seg.label, visible(got), visible(expect_text)))
        twin_note = None
        if seg.twin is False:
            twin_note = "this text box also has a legacy fallback copy that could not be paired; it was NOT edited"
        elif seg.twin is not None:
            if para_text(seg.twin) == seg.cur:
                para_replace(seg.twin, seg.cur, a, b, new, self.ox)
                if para_text(seg.twin) != expect_text:
                    raise SurgeryError("the fallback copy of %s did not take the edit" % seg.label)
                seg.twin_expected = expect_text
            else:
                twin_note = "this text box's legacy fallback copy differs from the visible text; it was NOT edited"
        return risk, twin_note

    def serialize(self):
        if self.stamp is not None:
            # D4 / doctrine rule 20: our build, never the last human's Office save -- lastModifiedBy = the build stamp,
            # modified = the build time, so share-check.sh reads it as BUILD, never as HUMAN EDIT or PRESTAMP.
            cp = self.document.core_properties
            cp.last_modified_by = self.stamp
            cp.modified = datetime.now(timezone.utc).replace(microsecond=0)
        buf = io.BytesIO()
        self.document.save(buf)
        return buf.getvalue()

    def expected(self):
        return [(s.label, s.cur, s.twin_expected) for s in self.segments]

    @staticmethod
    def extract(data):
        ox = load_docx()
        segs = collect_segments(ox["docx"].Document(io.BytesIO(data)), ox)
        return [(s.label, s.orig, s.twin_expected) for s in segs]


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Loading


class Edit(object):
    def __init__(self, **kw):
        self.__dict__.update(kw)


def load_edit_list(src):
    try:
        raw = sys.stdin.buffer.read() if src == "-" else read_bytes(src)
    except OSError as ex:
        raise BadInput("cannot read the edit list %s: %s" % (src, ex))
    try:
        data = json.loads(raw.decode("utf-8-sig"))
    except (UnicodeDecodeError, ValueError) as ex:
        raise BadInput("the edit list is not valid UTF-8 JSON: %s" % ex)
    deferred, rejected = [], []
    if isinstance(data, list):
        rows = data
    elif isinstance(data, dict):
        if "edits" not in data:
            raise BadInput("the edit list object has no 'edits' array")
        rows = data["edits"]
        deferred = data.get("deferred") if isinstance(data.get("deferred"), list) else []
        rejected = data.get("rejected") if isinstance(data.get("rejected"), list) else []
    else:
        raise BadInput("the edit list must be an object with 'edits' or a bare array of edits")
    if not isinstance(rows, list):
        raise BadInput("'edits' must be an array")
    edits, seen = [], set()
    for i, row in enumerate(rows):
        where = "edits[%d]" % i
        if not isinstance(row, dict):
            raise BadInput("%s is not an object" % where)
        eid = row.get("id")
        if not isinstance(eid, str) or not eid.strip():
            raise BadInput("%s: 'id' must be a non-empty string" % where)
        where = "edits[%d] (id %s)" % (i, eid)
        if eid in seen:
            raise BadInput("%s: duplicate id" % where)
        seen.add(eid)
        f = row.get("file")
        if not isinstance(f, str) or not f.strip():
            raise BadInput("%s: 'file' must be a non-empty string" % where)
        old, new = row.get("old"), row.get("new")
        if not isinstance(old, str) or old == "":
            raise BadInput("%s: 'old' must be a non-empty string" % where)
        if not isinstance(new, str):
            raise BadInput("%s: 'new' must be a string (\"\" deletes)" % where)
        for name, s in (("old", old), ("new", new)):
            try:
                s.encode("utf-8")
            except UnicodeEncodeError:
                raise BadInput("%s: '%s' contains a lone surrogate (invalid Unicode)" % (where, name))
        expect = row.get("expect", 1)
        expect = 1 if expect is None else expect
        if isinstance(expect, bool) or not isinstance(expect, int) or expect < 1:
            raise BadInput("%s: 'expect' must be an integer >= 1, got %r" % (where, expect))
        kind = row.get("kind")
        if kind is not None and kind not in ("mechanical", "judgment"):
            raise BadInput("%s: 'kind' must be 'mechanical' or 'judgment', got %r" % (where, kind))
        edits.append(Edit(index=i, id=eid, file=f, old=old, new=new, expect=expect, kind=kind, path=None, real=None))
    return edits, deferred, rejected


def open_doc(real):
    """(doc, data, None) or (None, None, reason)."""
    if not os.path.lexists(real) or not os.path.exists(real):
        return None, None, "file missing"
    if not os.path.isfile(real):
        return None, None, "not a regular file"
    try:
        data = read_bytes(real)
    except OSError as ex:
        return None, None, "cannot read: %s" % ex
    ext = os.path.splitext(real)[1].lower()
    if ext == ".docx":
        try:
            return DocxDoc(data), data, None
        except DocxUnavailable as ex:
            return None, None, str(ex)
        except Exception as ex:
            return None, None, "cannot open as .docx: %s: %s" % (type(ex).__name__, ex)
    if ext in UNSUPPORTED_EXT:
        return None, None, "unsupported file type %s: only UTF-8 text and .docx are edited" % ext
    if data[:4] == b"PK\x03\x04":
        return None, None, "zip container (%s): among Office formats only .docx is edited" % (ext or "no extension")
    if b"\x00" in data:
        return None, None, "binary file (contains NUL bytes): only UTF-8 text and .docx are edited"
    try:
        return TextDoc(data), data, None
    except UnicodeDecodeError as ex:
        return None, None, "not UTF-8 text (%s at byte %d): only UTF-8 text and .docx are edited" % (ex.reason, ex.start)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hints


def occurrence_list(doc, occ):
    locs = [doc.where(doc.segments[si], p) for si, p in occ[:MAX_LOCS]]
    more = " (+%d more)" % (len(occ) - MAX_LOCS) if len(occ) > MAX_LOCS else ""
    return "; ".join(locs) + more


def near_miss(doc, old):
    """The lowest normalisation level at which `old` is found: (level_name, [(seg, a, b)]) or None."""
    for level, name in LEVELS:
        nold, _ = norm_map(old, level)
        if not nold.strip():
            return None
        found = []
        for seg in doc.segments:
            ntext, idx = norm_map(seg.cur, level)
            for p in find_all(ntext, nold):
                found.append((seg, idx[p], idx[p + len(nold) - 1] + 1))
        if found:
            return name, found
    return None


def spans_paragraphs(doc, old):
    """.docx: old found only when paragraphs are joined (any whitespace/Unicode/case level) -> the labels it spans."""
    if doc.kind != "docx" or len(doc.segments) < 2:
        return None
    starts, joined = [], []
    pos = 0
    for seg in doc.segments:
        starts.append(pos)
        joined.append(seg.cur)
        pos += len(seg.cur) + 1
    text = "\n".join(joined)
    for level, _ in LEVELS:
        nold, _ = norm_map(old, level)
        ntext, idx = norm_map(text, level)
        p = ntext.find(nold) if nold.strip() else -1
        if p != -1:
            a, b = idx[p], idx[p + len(nold) - 1]
            sa = max(i for i, s in enumerate(starts) if s <= a)
            sb = max(i for i, s in enumerate(starts) if s <= b)
            if sa != sb:
                return doc.segments[sa].label, doc.segments[sb].label
            return None
    return None


def longest_prefix(doc, old):
    def found(k):
        return any(old[:k] in seg.cur for seg in doc.segments)

    if not found(1):
        return 0, None, None
    lo, hi = 1, len(old)
    while lo < hi:
        mid = (lo + hi + 1) // 2
        if found(mid):
            lo = mid
        else:
            hi = mid - 1
    for seg in doc.segments:
        p = seg.cur.find(old[:lo])
        if p != -1:
            return lo, seg, p
    return lo, None, None


def not_found_hint(doc, old, prior=()):
    writers = [p.id for p in prior if old in p.new]
    if writers:
        return ("old occurs in the `new` text of earlier edit %s; an edit never matches text another edit writes "
                "-- fold this change into %s" % (", ".join(writers), writers[0]))
    nm = near_miss(doc, old)
    if nm:
        name, found = nm
        seg, a, b = found[0]
        actual = seg.cur[a:b]
        return ("near miss after %s normalisation: %d match(es), first at %s, where the file has %s; %s. "
                "NOT applied -- matching is exact; copy `old` from the file byte for byte"
                % (name, len(found), doc.where(seg, a), visible(actual), first_diff(old, actual)))
    span = spans_paragraphs(doc, old)
    if span:
        return ("old spans a paragraph break (%s -> %s); .docx edits match within one paragraph -- split it into "
                "one edit per paragraph" % span)
    k, seg, p = longest_prefix(doc, old)
    if seg is not None and k >= max(8, len(old) // 4):
        nxt = seg.cur[p + k] if p + k < len(seg.cur) else None
        return ("no near match; the longest prefix of old found in the file is %d of %d chars (at %s), then old has "
                "%s and the file has %s" % (k, len(old), doc.where(seg, p), cname(old[k]),
                                            cname(nxt) if nxt is not None else "end of text"))
    return "no near match and no substantial prefix of old occurs in this file -- is `file` the right target?"


def consumed_by(doc, old):
    """Earlier edits whose replaced ORIGINAL text intersects an original occurrence of `old`."""
    ids = []
    for seg in doc.segments:
        for p in find_all(seg.orig, old):
            for (o_start, o_end, new, eid) in seg.reps:
                if p < o_end and o_start < p + len(old) and eid not in ids:
                    ids.append(eid)
    return ids


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Report


class Report(object):
    def __init__(self, mode, dry_run):
        self.mode, self.dry_run = mode, dry_run
        self.misses, self.matched, self.applied = [], [], []
        self.files_changed, self.backups, self.outputs = [], [], []
        self.formatting_risk, self.warnings = [], []
        self.missed_ids = set()
        self.written = False
        self.counts = {}
        self.stamp = None

    def miss(self, e, reason, hint=None, path=None):
        row = {"id": e.id, "file": path or e.path, "reason": reason}
        if hint:
            row["hint"] = hint
        self.misses.append(row)
        self.missed_ids.add(e.id)

    def as_dict(self, extra=None):
        d = {"ok": not self.misses and not (extra or {}).get("error"), "mode": self.mode, "dry_run": self.dry_run,
             "written": self.written, "stamp": self.stamp, "applied": self.applied, "misses": self.misses,
             "files_changed": self.files_changed, "backups": self.backups, "matched": self.matched,
             "outputs": self.outputs, "formatting_risk": self.formatting_risk, "warnings": self.warnings,
             "counts": self.counts}
        if extra:
            d.update(extra)
        return d


def _err(line):
    enc = getattr(sys.stderr, "encoding", None) or "utf-8"
    sys.stderr.write(line.encode(enc, "backslashreplace").decode(enc, "replace") + "\n")


def _out(obj):
    try:
        sys.stdout.write(json.dumps(obj, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
    except UnicodeEncodeError:
        sys.stdout.write(json.dumps(obj, indent=2, ensure_ascii=True) + "\n")
    sys.stdout.flush()


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Applying


def apply_file(doc, edits, rep, path):
    applied = []
    for e in edits:
        if doc.broken:
            rep.miss(e, "not attempted: edit %s failed inside this file and the file was abandoned" % doc.broken)
            continue
        if e.kind == "judgment":
            rep.miss(e, "kind is 'judgment': a named human decides it, so it is never applied mechanically "
                        "(judgment rows go to the owner queue with both values, not into edits[])")
            continue
        if e.old == e.new:
            rep.miss(e, "no-op: new is identical to old, so nothing would change (the no-op-fix class)")
            continue
        if doc.kind == "docx":
            bad = xml_bad_char(e.new)
            if bad is not None:
                rep.miss(e, "new contains %s, which a .docx (XML) cannot hold" % cname(bad))
                continue
        L = len(e.old)
        occ = [(si, p) for si, seg in enumerate(doc.segments) for p in find_all(seg.cur, e.old)]
        n = len(occ)
        if any(s1 == s2 and p2 < p1 + L for (s1, p1), (s2, p2) in zip(occ, occ[1:])):
            rep.miss(e, "ambiguous: old occurs %d times with overlapping matches (like 'aa' in 'aaa')" % n,
                     hint="occurrences at %s; lengthen old so its matches cannot overlap" % occurrence_list(doc, occ))
            continue
        if n != e.expect:
            orig_n = sum(len(find_all(s.orig, e.old)) for s in doc.segments)
            consumed = consumed_by(doc, e.old)
            if consumed:
                reason = ("overlaps an earlier edit: %s changed text that old matched in the original (original %d "
                          "occurrence(s), now %d, expect %d); never chained or fuzzy-matched"
                          % (", ".join(consumed), orig_n, n, e.expect))
                hint = ("re-anchor this edit on the text as it reads after %s, or fold it into %s"
                        % (", ".join(consumed), consumed[0]))
            elif n == 0:
                reason, hint = "not found", not_found_hint(doc, e.old, edits[:edits.index(e)])
            else:
                reason = "found %d occurrences != expect %d" % (n, e.expect)
                hint = ("occurrences at %s; %s" % (occurrence_list(doc, occ),
                        "lengthen old with neighbouring text so it is unique, or set expect to %d if every one "
                        "must change" % n if n > e.expect else "expect is higher than the file supports"))
            rep.miss(e, reason, hint=hint)
            continue
        hits = []
        for si, p in occ:
            for (c, d, eid) in doc.segments[si].dirty():
                if ((c < d and p < d and c < p + L) or (c == d and p < c < p + L)) and eid not in hits:
                    hits.append(eid)
        if hits:
            rep.miss(e, "overlaps an earlier edit: the match falls on text written by %s; never chained"
                     % ", ".join(hits),
                     hint="old must match the file as it reads BEFORE this list; merge this change into %s" % hits[0])
            continue
        orig_n = sum(len(find_all(s.orig, e.old)) for s in doc.segments)
        if orig_n != n:
            rep.warnings.append("%s: the original had %d occurrence(s) of old; after earlier edits %d remained and %s "
                                "edited -- confirm the list order was intended" % (e.id, orig_n, n,
                                                                                 "was" if n == 1 else "were"))
        by_seg = {}
        for si, p in occ:
            by_seg.setdefault(si, []).append(p)
        try:
            for si in sorted(by_seg):
                seg = doc.segments[si]
                for p in sorted(by_seg[si], reverse=True):
                    risk, twin_note = doc.edit(seg, p, p + L, e.new)
                    seg.replace(p, p + L, e.new, e.id)
                    if risk or twin_note:
                        rep.formatting_risk.append(_risk_row(e, path, seg, risk, twin_note))
        except (SurgeryError, ValueError) as ex:
            rep.miss(e, "internal .docx edit failed (%s); the file is abandoned and nothing will be written" % ex)
            doc.broken = e.id
            continue
        applied.append(e)
    return applied


def _risk_row(e, path, seg, risk, twin_note):
    parts = []
    row = {"id": e.id, "file": path, "location": seg.label, "runs": 1, "same_formatting": True}
    if risk:
        row["runs"], row["same_formatting"] = risk["runs"], risk["same_formatting"]
        if risk["runs"] > 1:
            parts.append("match spans %d runs; the new text takes the first run's formatting (%s)"
                         % (risk["runs"], "the runs' formatting is identical" if risk["same_formatting"]
                            else "their formatting DIFFERS -- check bold/italic/size"))
        if risk["boundary"]:
            parts.append("the match crosses a hyperlink / field / content-control / tracked-change boundary")
        if risk["embedded"]:
            parts.append("non-text content inside the match was kept in place: %s" % ", ".join(risk["embedded"]))
    if twin_note:
        parts.append(twin_note)
    row["detail"] = "; ".join(parts)
    return row


def verify(doc, data, applied):
    """Re-extract `data` and compare it with the model: [(edit or None, message)]; empty = verified."""
    try:
        got = doc.extract(data)
    except Exception as ex:
        return [(None, "cannot re-read the rebuilt file: %s: %s" % (type(ex).__name__, ex))]
    exp = doc.expected()
    problems = []
    if len(got) != len(exp):
        problems.append((None, "the rebuilt file has %d text units, expected %d" % (len(got), len(exp))))
    else:
        diffs = [(g, x) for g, x in zip(got, exp) if g[1] != x[1] or (x[2] is not None and g[2] != x[2])]
        for g, x in diffs[:3]:
            which = "fallback copy of " if g[1] == x[1] else ""
            problems.append((None, "rebuilt text differs at %s%s: expected %s, got %s"
                             % (which, x[0] or "the file", visible(x[2] if which else x[1]),
                                visible(g[2] if which else g[1]))))
    for seg in doc.segments:
        if seg.rebuilt() != seg.cur:
            problems.append((None, "internal: the replacement ledger does not reproduce the text of %s"
                             % (seg.label or "the file")))
    texts = [g[1] for g in got]
    for e in applied:
        needle, label = (e.new, "new") if e.new else (e.old, "old (deletion)")
        want = sum(len(find_all(seg.cur, needle)) for seg in doc.segments)
        have = sum(len(find_all(t, needle)) for t in texts)
        if e.new and want < e.expect:
            problems.append((e, "new is present %d time(s) in the expected text, fewer than expect %d" % (want, e.expect)))
        if have != want:
            problems.append((e, "%s is present %d time(s) in the rebuilt file, expected %d" % (label, have, want)))
    return problems


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Writing (only ever after a clean pre-write verification; backups before any overwrite)


def dir_creatable(d):
    p = d
    while not os.path.exists(p):
        parent = os.path.dirname(p)
        if parent == p:
            return False
        p = parent
    return os.path.isdir(p) and os.access(p, os.W_OK | os.X_OK)


def word_lock(path):
    """A Word owner file (~$name / ~$me / ~$ame) beside `path` means the document is open in Word."""
    d, name = os.path.split(path)
    try:
        entries = os.listdir(d)
    except OSError:
        return None
    for ent in entries:
        if ent.startswith("~$") and len(ent) > 2:
            rest = ent[2:]
            if rest == name or (len(name) > 1 and rest == name[1:]) or (len(name) > 2 and rest == name[2:]):
                return os.path.join(d, ent)
    return None


def _write_backup(data, stat_src, base_path):
    """Write `data` to base_path (or base_path-2, -3, ... -- an existing backup is never overwritten), then verify."""
    d = os.path.dirname(base_path)
    os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
    path, n = base_path, 1
    while True:
        try:
            fd = os.open(path, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL, 0o600)
            break
        except FileExistsError:
            n += 1
            path = "%s-%d" % (base_path, n)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "wb") as fh:
        fh.write(data)
        fh.flush()
        os.fsync(fh.fileno())
    shutil.copystat(stat_src, path)
    if read_bytes(path) != data:
        raise OSError("backup %s does not read back byte-identical" % path)
    return path


def _write_atomic(dest, data, mode_src):
    d = os.path.dirname(dest)
    os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=".apply-edits-", suffix=".tmp", dir=d)
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "wb") as fh:
            fh.write(data)
            fh.flush()
            os.fsync(fh.fileno())
        shutil.copymode(mode_src, tmp)
        os.replace(tmp, dest)
    except BaseException:
        if os.path.exists(tmp):
            os.unlink(tmp)   # our own temp file, never user data
        raise


def _backup_base(target, rel_base, backup_dir, ts):
    if backup_dir:
        return os.path.join(backup_dir, os.path.relpath(target, rel_base)) + ".bak-" + ts
    return target + ".bak-" + ts


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Main


def parse_args(argv):
    ap = _Parser(prog="apply-edits", description="Apply an EDIT_LIST exactly (see the header of this file).")
    ap.add_argument("edit_list", help="EDIT_LIST JSON file, or - for stdin")
    ap.add_argument("--out-dir", help="write edited copies under this directory (non-destructive)")
    ap.add_argument("--in-place", action="store_true", help="edit the files themselves, after dated backups")
    ap.add_argument("--backup-dir", help="put backups here (mirrored paths) instead of beside each file")
    ap.add_argument("--root", help="resolve relative `file` paths here; mirror outputs relative to it")
    ap.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="compute and report, write nothing")
    ap.add_argument("--stamp", help="lastModifiedBy for every .docx written (one of share-check.sh's BUILD_STAMPS for a "
                                    "Acme payer build); required when a .docx is written")
    args = ap.parse_args(argv)
    if args.out_dir and args.in_place:
        raise BadInput("choose one of --out-dir DIR or --in-place, not both")
    if not args.out_dir and not args.in_place and not args.dry_run:
        raise BadInput("choose --out-dir DIR (non-destructive), --in-place (with dated backups) or --dry-run")
    if args.backup_dir and not (args.out_dir or args.in_place):
        raise BadInput("--backup-dir needs --out-dir or --in-place")
    return args


def _real(p):
    return os.path.realpath(os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(p)))


def _words(texts):
    return sum(len(t.split()) for t in texts)


def run(argv):
    """Returns the Report; raises BadInput / Refused (the latter carrying the partial report as .report)."""
    args = parse_args(argv)
    mode = "in-place" if args.in_place else ("out-dir" if args.out_dir else "check")
    rep = Report(mode, bool(args.dry_run))
    try:
        return _run(args, mode, rep)
    except Refused as ex:
        ex.report = rep
        raise


def _run(args, mode, rep):
    edits, deferred, rejected = load_edit_list(args.edit_list)
    root = _real(args.root) if args.root else None
    if root and not os.path.isdir(root):
        raise BadInput("--root %s is not a directory" % args.root)
    for e in edits:
        p = os.path.expanduser(e.file)
        e.path = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(root or os.getcwd(), p))
        e.real = os.path.realpath(e.path)
        if root and os.path.commonpath([root, e.real]) != root:
            raise BadInput("edit %s: %s is outside --root %s" % (e.id, e.file, root))
    groups = {}
    for e in edits:
        groups.setdefault(e.real, []).append(e)
    base = root or (os.path.commonpath([os.path.dirname(r) for r in groups]) if groups else os.getcwd())
    out_dir = _real(args.out_dir) if args.out_dir else None
    backup_dir = _real(args.backup_dir) if args.backup_dir else None
    dest = {}
    for real in groups:
        if mode == "out-dir":
            dest[real] = os.path.join(out_dir, os.path.relpath(real, base))
            if dest[real] in groups:
                raise BadInput("--out-dir %s would overwrite the source file %s; use another directory or --in-place"
                               % (args.out_dir, dest[real]))
        else:
            dest[real] = real
    ts = _timestamp()
    rep.counts = {"edits": len(edits), "files": len(groups), "deferred": len(deferred), "rejected": len(rejected)}
    if not edits:
        rep.warnings.append("the edit list has no edits; nothing to apply")
    # D4: a .docx this run writes carries a build stamp, never the last human's name. Checked before any work.
    has_docx = any(real.lower().endswith(".docx") for real in groups)
    writes = mode != "check" and not args.dry_run
    check_stamp(args.stamp, has_docx and writes, rep)
    rep.stamp = args.stamp
    if has_docx and not writes and args.stamp is None:
        rep.warnings.append("this list edits a .docx: the real run needs --stamp (share-check.sh's BUILD_STAMPS for a "
                            "Acme payer build)")
    if args.stamp is not None and not has_docx:
        rep.warnings.append("--stamp applies to .docx outputs only; this list edits none")

    # Read-only preflight: refuse before any work if a write would be impossible or unsafe.
    if mode == "in-place":
        for real in groups:
            if os.path.isfile(real):
                bdir = os.path.dirname(_backup_base(real, base, backup_dir, ts))
                if not dir_creatable(bdir):
                    raise Refused("cannot write a backup of %s into %s; --in-place never runs without one"
                                  % (real, bdir))
                if not os.access(real, os.W_OK) or not dir_creatable(os.path.dirname(real)):
                    raise Refused("%s is read-only (or its folder is); --in-place will not replace it" % real)
                lock = word_lock(real) if real.lower().endswith(".docx") else None
                if lock:
                    raise Refused("%s is open in Word (%s); close it first -- nothing was written" % (real, lock))
    elif mode == "out-dir":
        if backup_dir and not dir_creatable(backup_dir):
            raise Refused("cannot create --backup-dir %s" % backup_dir)
        for real in groups:
            if not dir_creatable(os.path.dirname(dest[real])):
                raise Refused("cannot create %s for the edited copy of %s" % (os.path.dirname(dest[real]), real))

    # Apply in memory.
    docs = {}
    for real, es in groups.items():
        doc, data, err = open_doc(real)
        if err:
            for e in es:
                rep.miss(e, "%s: %s" % (err, e.path) if err == "file missing" else err)
            continue
        if mode == "out-dir" and real.lower().endswith(".docx") and word_lock(real):
            rep.warnings.append("%s is open in Word (lock file present): edits were applied to its last SAVED "
                                "version" % real)
        if doc.kind == "docx":
            doc.stamp = args.stamp
        applied = apply_file(doc, es, rep, es[0].path)
        docs[real] = (doc, data, applied, es[0].path)
    for real, (doc, data, applied, path) in docs.items():
        for e in applied:
            rep.matched.append(e.id)

    # Pre-write verification: serialise, re-extract the SAME bytes, compare with the model.
    planned = []
    for real, (doc, data, applied, path) in docs.items():
        if not applied or doc.broken:
            continue
        new_bytes = doc.serialize()
        for e, msg in verify(doc, new_bytes, applied):
            for x in ([e] if e is not None else applied):
                if x.id not in rep.missed_ids:
                    rep.miss(x, "post-check (pre-write): " + msg, path=path)
        planned.append({"real": real, "path": path, "dest": dest[real], "old": data, "new": new_bytes,
                        "applied": applied, "doc": doc,
                        "row": {"file": path, "output": dest[real] if mode != "check" else None,
                                "status": "planned", "md5_before": md5(data), "md5_after": md5(new_bytes),
                                "chars_before": sum(len(s.orig) for s in doc.segments),
                                "chars_after": sum(len(s.cur) for s in doc.segments),
                                "words_before": _words([s.orig for s in doc.segments]),
                                "words_after": _words([s.cur for s in doc.segments]),
                                **({"stamped": doc.stamp is not None} if doc.kind == "docx" else {})}})
    rep.matched = [i for i in rep.matched if i not in rep.missed_ids]
    rep.outputs = [p["row"] for p in planned]
    order = {e.id: e.index for e in edits}
    rep.misses.sort(key=lambda m: order.get(m["id"], 0))

    if rep.misses or args.dry_run or mode == "check":
        return rep

    # Write phase: preconditions for every target, then every backup, then every write.
    for p in planned:
        if os.path.exists(p["dest"]):
            current = read_bytes(p["dest"])
            if mode == "in-place" and current != p["old"]:
                raise Refused("%s changed on disk after it was read (another writer?); nothing was written"
                              % p["dest"])
            if current == p["new"]:
                p["row"]["status"] = "unchanged"
                p["skip"] = True
                continue
            if p["dest"].lower().endswith(".docx") and word_lock(p["dest"]):
                raise Refused("%s is open in Word (%s); nothing was written" % (p["dest"], word_lock(p["dest"])))
            p["backup_of"] = current
    for p in planned:
        if "backup_of" in p:
            rel_base = base if mode == "in-place" else out_dir
            try:
                bpath = _write_backup(p["backup_of"], p["dest"], _backup_base(p["dest"], rel_base, backup_dir, ts))
            except OSError as ex:
                raise Refused("could not write a verified backup of %s (%s); nothing was overwritten" % (p["dest"], ex))
            rep.backups.append({"file": p["dest"], "backup": bpath})
    failed = None
    for p in planned:
        if p.get("skip"):
            continue
        if failed:
            p["row"]["status"] = "not written"
            for e in p["applied"]:
                rep.miss(e, "not written: writing %s failed first" % failed, path=p["path"])
            continue
        try:
            _write_atomic(p["dest"], p["new"], p["real"])
        except OSError as ex:
            failed = p["dest"]
            p["row"]["status"] = "write failed"
            for e in p["applied"]:
                rep.miss(e, "write failed for %s: %s" % (p["dest"], ex), path=p["path"])
            continue
        rep.written = True
        p["row"]["status"] = "written"
        rep.files_changed.append(p["path"])

    # Post-check from disk: the bytes must be what was written, and re-extract to the expected text.
    for p in planned:
        if p["row"]["status"] not in ("written", "unchanged"):
            continue
        try:
            disk = read_bytes(p["dest"])
        except OSError as ex:
            disk = None
            problems = [(None, "cannot re-read %s: %s" % (p["dest"], ex))]
        if disk is not None:
            problems = [] if disk == p["new"] else [(None, "the bytes on disk differ from the bytes written")]
            problems += verify(p["doc"], disk, p["applied"])
        for e, msg in problems:
            for x in ([e] if e is not None else p["applied"]):
                if x.id not in rep.missed_ids:
                    rep.miss(x, "post-check: %s (%s)" % (msg, p["dest"]), path=p["path"])
        for e in p["applied"]:
            if e.id not in rep.missed_ids:
                rep.applied.append(e.id)
    rep.applied.sort(key=lambda i: order.get(i, 0))
    rep.misses.sort(key=lambda m: order.get(m["id"], 0))
    return rep


def main(argv=None):
    argv = sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv
    try:
        rep = run(argv)
    except BadInput as ex:
        _out({"ok": False, "exit": EXIT_BAD, "error": "bad input: %s" % ex, "applied": [], "misses": [],
              "files_changed": [], "backups": []})
        _err("BAD INPUT: %s" % ex)
        return EXIT_BAD
    except Refused as ex:
        partial = getattr(ex, "report", None)
        body = partial.as_dict() if partial else {"applied": [], "misses": [], "files_changed": [], "backups": []}
        body.update({"ok": False, "exit": EXIT_BAD, "error": "refused: %s" % ex, "written": False, "applied": []})
        _out(body)
        for b in body.get("backups", []):
            _err("BACKUP kept %s -> %s" % (b["file"], b["backup"]))
        _err("REFUSED: %s" % ex)
        return EXIT_BAD
    n = len(rep.misses)
    code = EXIT_MISS if n else EXIT_OK
    rep.counts.update({"applied": len(rep.applied), "matched": len(rep.matched), "misses": n,
                       "formatting_risk": len(rep.formatting_risk)})
    _out(rep.as_dict({"exit": code}))
    for m in rep.misses:
        _err("MISS %s %s: %s" % (m["id"], m["file"], m["reason"]))
        if m.get("hint"):
            _err("  hint: %s" % m["hint"])
    for r in rep.formatting_risk:
        _err("RISK %s %s: %s" % (r["id"], r["location"], r["detail"]))
    for w in rep.warnings:
        _err("WARNING %s" % w)
    if rep.written:
        _err("apply-edits %s: %d applied and post-checked, %d file(s) written, %d backup(s)"
             % (rep.mode, len(rep.applied), len(rep.files_changed), len(rep.backups)))
    else:
        why = "dry run" if rep.dry_run or rep.mode == "check" else ("a miss aborts the whole list" if n else "no changes")
        _err("apply-edits %s: %d of %d edit(s) matched; NOTHING written (%s)"
             % (rep.mode, len(rep.matched), rep.counts.get("edits", 0), why))
    _err("MISSES (%d)" % n)
    return code


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
